# data/raw/, data/processed/, data/fixtures/ and outputs/ are deliberately NOT
# ignored. They were un-ignored by team decision so a fresh clone has the
# dataset and the generated artefacts without re-running collection. Two costs
# come with that: every run produces a large binary diff, and data/raw/ holds
# third-party brand assets (page captures and screenshots) that were never
# meant for redistribution - confirm that is still acceptable before pushing
# them anywhere public. These rules are one revert away.
